hey deal with your rubbish, and you get meat.&nbsp;</p>',NULL,NULL,0,1789447730,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15912,1529,3770,6900,9,9,'multiple_choice','It does not make sense to give up meat without giving up dairy products too.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'E',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"A\":\"A\",\"B\":\"B\",\"C\":\"C\",\"D\":\"D\",\"E\":\"E\"}',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'<p>E. In some parts of the world today, livestock such as chickens can subsist on leftovers and whatever they find. Tara Garnett, who heads the Food Climate Research Network at the University of Surrey, points out the usefulness of these animals. By giving them your leftovers, she says, they deal with your rubbish, and you get meat.&nbsp;</p>',NULL,NULL,0,1789447730,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15913,1529,3770,6900,10,10,'multiple_choice','Some animals can be fed in a way that allows waste to be recycled.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'B',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"A\":\"A\",\"B\":\"B\",\"C\":\"C\",\"D\":\"D\",\"E\":\"E\"}',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'<p>E. In some parts of the world today, livestock such as chickens can subsist on leftovers and whatever they find. Tara Garnett, who heads the Food Climate Research Network at the University of Surrey, points out the usefulness of these animals. By giving them your leftovers, she says, they deal with your rubbish, and you get meat.&nbsp;</p>',NULL,NULL,0,1789447730,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15914,1529,3771,6901,11,11,'multiple_choice','Experiencing small doses of anxiety can',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"A\":\"A\",\"B\":\"B\",\"C\":\"C\",\"D\":\"D\",\"E\":\"E\"}',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'This one is eplained for all',NULL,NULL,0,1789447730,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15915,1529,3771,6901,12,12,'multiple_choice','Imagining or exaggerating problems can',NULL,NULL,NULL,'C',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"A\":\"A\",\"B\":\"B\",\"C\":\"C\",\"D\":\"D\",\"E\":\"E\"}',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'This one is eplained for all',NULL,NULL,0,1789447730,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15916,1529,3771,6901,13,13,'multiple_choice','Nearly one in five people can',NULL,NULL,NULL,'D',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"A\":\"A\",\"B\":\"B\",\"C\":\"C\",\"D\":\"D\",\"E\":\"E\"}',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'This one is eplained for all',NULL,NULL,0,1789447730,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15939,1532,3776,6906,1,1,'sentence_completion','Huxley formulated his theory while studying a dinosaur belonging to a group called&nbsp; ___ .',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[[\"theropods\"]]',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'<div>Vị trí thông tin (Đoạn 2): \"He knew he was dealing with the lower leg bone (tibia) of a meat-eating, two-legged dinosaur belonging to the classification known as theropods...\"</div><div><br></div><div>Giải thích: Bài đọc đề cập Huxley nghiên cứu xương cẳng chân của một loài khủng long thuộc phân loại (classification/group) được gọi là theropods.</div>',NULL,NULL,0,1789653679,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15940,1532,3776,6906,2,2,'sentence_completion','Heilmann rejected Huxley’s theory because of the apparent absence of 2 ___ in dinosaurs.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[[\"collarbones\"]]',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'<li><p><b>Vị trí thông tin (Đoạn 3):</b> \"Heilmann had noted that two-legged, meat-eating dinosaurs lacked <b>collarbones</b>.\"</p></li><li><p><b>Giải thích:</b> Heilmann bác bỏ lý thuyết của Huxley vì nhận thấy khủng long dường như thiếu (lacked / apparent absence) xương đòn (<b>collarbones</b>).</p></li>',NULL,NULL,0,1789653679,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15941,1532,3776,6906,3,3,'sentence_completion','Feduccia and Martin believe that the ancestor of today’s birds was a kind of early 3 ___ .&nbsp;',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[[\"reptile\"]]',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'<div>Vị trí thông tin (Đoạn 5): \"They contend that birds evolved from some unknown reptile at a time long before dinosaurs.\"</div><div><br></div><div>Giải thích: Feduccia và Martin cho rằng tổ tiên loài chim là một loài bò sát cổ đại (reptile) chưa được biết đến.</div>',NULL,NULL,0,1789653679,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15942,1532,3776,6906,4,4,'sentence_completion','In cladistics, the 4 ___ between organisms’ characteristics are of major importance.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[[\"similarities\"]]',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'<div>Vị trí thông tin (Đoạn 5): \"Supporters of cladistics, however, maintain that differences between organisms do not matter, as it is the similarities between them that count.\"</div><div><br></div><div>Giải thích: Trong phân loại học cladistics, điều quan trọng (major importance / count) giữa các đặc điểm của sinh vật chính là sự tương đồng (similarities).</div>',NULL,NULL,0,1789653679,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15943,1532,3776,6906,5,5,'sentence_completion','The dangerous 5 ___ on a primitive bird from Madagascar adds weight to the ‘dino-bird’ argument.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[[\"claw\"]]',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'<li><p><b>Vị trí thông tin (Đoạn 7):</b> \"And Rahonavis, a primitive bird from Madagascar is more bird-like than Archaeopteryx, yet retains some distinctive dinosaur features, including a long and vicious <b>claw</b> at the end of its wing.\"</p></li><li><p><b>Giải thích:</b> Bài đọc nhắc tới loài chim cổ từ Madagascar (Rahonavis) sở hữu một móng vuốt hung dữ/nguy hiểm (vicious / dangerous) là <b>claw</b> ở đầu cánh.</p></li>',NULL,NULL,0,1789653679,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15944,1532,3777,6907,6,6,'note_completion','<div>When uranium was discovered to be radioactive, Marie Curie found that the element called ___ had the same property.</div>',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[[\"thorium\"]]',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'<div>Vị trí thông tin (Đoạn 1): \"...Marie Curie decided to find out if the radioactivity discovered in uranium was to be found in other elements. She discovered that this was true for thorium.\"</div><div><br></div><div>Giải thích: Marie Curie muốn tìm xem tính phóng xạ trong uranium có ở các nguyên tố khác không, và bà phát hiện điều này đúng với thorium.</div>',NULL,NULL,0,1789653679,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15945,1532,3777,6907,7,7,'note_completion','Marie and Pierre Curie’s research into the radioactivity of the mineral known as ___ led to the discovery of two new elements.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[[\"pitchblende\"]]',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'<li><p><b>Vị trí thông tin (Đoạn 2):</b> \"Turning her attention to minerals, she found her interest drawn to <b>pitchblende</b>... Pierre Curie joined her... and that led to the discovery of the new elements, polonium and radium.\"</p></li><li><p><b>Giải thích:</b> Việc nghiên cứu khoáng vật <b>pitchblende</b> đã dẫn đến sự phát hiện hai nguyên tố mới là polonium và radium.</p></li>',NULL,NULL,0,1789653679,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15946,1532,3777,6907,8,8,'note_completion','In 1911, Marie Curie received recognition for her work on the element ___ .&nbsp;',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[[\"radium\"]]',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'<div>Vị trí thông tin (Đoạn 4): \"In 1911 she was awarded the Nobel Prize for Chemistry for the isolation of a pure form of radium.\"</div><div><br></div><div>Giải thích: Năm 1911, bà nhận giải Nobel Hóa học nhờ thành tựu cô lập dạng tinh khiết của nguyên tố radium.</div>',NULL,NULL,0,1789653679,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15947,1532,3777,6907,9,9,'note_completion','Marie and Irène Curie developed X-radiography which was used as a medical technique for 4 ____',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[[\"soldiers\"]]',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'<div>Vị trí thông tin (Đoạn 5): \"...Marie Curie, with the help of her daughter Irène, devoted herself to the development of the use of X-radiography... used for the treatment of wounded soldiers.\"</div><div><br></div><div>Giải thích: Kỹ thuật X-quang được dùng làm phương pháp y tế để điều trị cho những người lính bị thương (soldiers).</div>',NULL,NULL,0,1789653679,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15948,1532,3777,6907,10,10,'note_completion','Marie Curie saw the importance of collecting radioactive material both for research and for cases of 5 ___.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[[\"illness\"]]',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'Vị trí thông tin (Đoạn 7): \"One of Marie Curie’s outstanding achievements was to have understood the need to accumulate intense radioactive sources, not only to treat illness but also to maintain an abundant supply for research.\"<div><br></div><div>Giải thích: Bà hiểu tầm quan trọng của việc tích trữ nguồn phóng xạ không chỉ cho nghiên cứu mà còn để điều trị bệnh tật (illness).</div>',NULL,NULL,0,1789653679,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15949,1532,3777,6907,11,11,'note_completion','The radioactive material stocked in Paris contributed to the discoveries in the 1930s of the&nbsp; ___',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[[\"neutron\"]]',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'<div>Vị trí thông tin (Đoạn 7): \"This work prepared the way for the discovery of the neutron by Sir James Chadwick and, above all, for the discovery in 1934 by Irène and Frédéric Joliot-Curie of artificial radioactivity.\"</div><div><br></div><div>Giải thích: Lượng phóng xạ lưu trữ ở Paris đã đóng góp vào phát minh ra hạt neutron và hiện tượng phóng xạ nhân tạo trong những năm 1930.</div>',NULL,NULL,0,1789653679,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15950,1533,3778,6908,1,1,'multiple_choice','test',NULL,NULL,NULL,'False',NULL,NULL,'{\"title\":\"c\\u00e2u 1\"}','[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'test',NULL,NULL,0,1789658112,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15951,1533,3778,6908,2,2,'multiple_choice','test',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Not Given',NULL,NULL,'{\"title\":\"C\\u00e2u 2\"}','[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'test',NULL,NULL,0,1789658112,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15952,1533,3778,6908,3,3,'multiple_choice','test',NULL,NULL,NULL,'True',NULL,NULL,'{\"title\":\"C\\u00e2u 3\"}','[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'test',NULL,NULL,0,1789658112,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15956,1535,3780,6910,1,1,'multiple_choice','Traffic accidents are sometimes caused by lack of sleep.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'C',NULL,NULL,'{\"title\":\"Question 1\"}','{\"A\":\"A\",\"B\":\"B\",\"C\":\"C\",\"D\":\"D\",\"E\":\"E\",\"F\":\"F\"}',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.2,1,NULL,'<ul style=\"margin: 0px; lis